                <div class="doc-content">
                    <div class="doc-item">
                        <h2>Advanced Integration</h2>
                        <p>ContainEye bridges the gap between your server and your device ecosystem with SFTP files, the Agentic AI assistant, and Apple Shortcuts.</p>

                        <div class="screenshot-box">
                            <img src="/images/containeye-framed/sftp-connected.png" alt="SFTP browser">
                        </div>

                        <h3>SFTP Files</h3>
                        <p>Browse your server's files over SFTP using the same credentials as SSH: go up and down directories, navigate to a path, toggle hidden files, upload (multi-select with progress), create folders and files, rename or delete, and export or open any file — including a full-screen text editor that saves changes straight back to the server. From the terminal, pressing Enter after <code>open</code>/<code>nano</code>/<code>vim</code>/<code>nvim &lt;file&gt;</code> can open the file right in this editor.</p>

                        <h3>Agentic AI Assistant</h3>
                        <p>A conversational assistant that lists your servers, runs approved commands, reads and writes files, and creates or updates tests and snippets for you — with every server command going through an approval dialog (<strong>Allow Once</strong>, <strong>Always Allow "…" Commands</strong>, <strong>Always Allow All Commands</strong>, <strong>Deny</strong>, <strong>Cancel</strong>) unless you allow it permanently.</p>

                        <h3>Power Automations</h3>
                        <p>Trigger server tests with the <strong>Test Servers</strong> and <strong>Run a single Test</strong> Shortcuts actions — they run in the background without opening the app, so you can schedule them by time of day, location, or other automations. The home-screen <strong>Test Widget</strong> shows your most important test and re-runs it in one tap. All connections are direct and native.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
